      {
        "id": 243019,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2022-03-01T13:34:37.837Z",
        "cooked": "<p>To answer my summons: The Sentinels Wiki is basically Lynkfox having installed the Mediawiki software on his own web server space. It’s not difficult for anyone with a moderate amount of PHP and web knowledge, but as FrivYeti noted it is time-consuming and costs some money.</p>\n<p>Would something like Google Docs or Dropbox Paper be sufficient for this purpose? It’s not quite as fancy-looking or convenient as a wiki would be, but it seems like it would work well for minimal time/money investment cost.</p>",
